speechtext:
I do not think we should be so narrow-minded as to confine all our attention to one little town on the map. It may be a nice little place;
I am not trying to cast any reflections on it, but there are many more important places in Canada.
Within the last little while I have heard the Minister of Munitions and Supply say there was a shortage of steel. I do not believe that. I think that statement is absolutely incorrect, and I am going to tell you why. The rolling mills in Calgary quit work at five o'clock every afternoon. One of the men in the factory told me that they could produce three times the supply that they are producing.
